The synthesis report shown is always the same baseline (640243 cycles, static arrays) regardless of which version was submitted. The persistent problems are:

1. **`static` arrays** → cosim failure (state persists between calls)
2. **Memory port conflicts** → the 5-point stencil accesses rows `i-1`, `i`, `i+1` simultaneously, requiring partitioning on dim=1 to separate those rows into different banks

The key insight: with the inner `j` loop pipelined, each cycle accesses `lA[i-1][j]`, `lA[i][j]`, `lA[i+1][j]` — three different row indices. Without dim=1 partitioning, these map to the same BRAM port and serialize. Adding `cyclic factor=3` on dim=1 ensures rows `i-1 % 3`, `i % 3`, `(i+1) % 3` are always in different banks.

